@title Customer Advisory Council Charter
@subtitle Windrow Software. Effective 2027-01-01.
@author Sponsor: Ines Carvalho, Chief Product Officer
@date 2027-01-01

## Purpose

The Customer Advisory Council gives customers a structured, regular way to shape the Windrow product roadmap and to tell us plainly what is not working.

## Membership

- The council has 14 seats: 12 customer members and 2 Windrow product leads.
- Customer members are chosen to reflect the customer base by company size and industry.
- Customer members serve two-year terms, renewable once.
- Half of the customer seats rotate each year, so that the council keeps continuity.
- The chair is Ines Carvalho. The vice chair is elected by the customer members.

## Meetings

The council meets quarterly, for two hours each time.

table = Meeting,Date; Q1,2027-03-10; Q2,2027-06-09; Q3,2027-09-08; Q4,2027-12-08

- The agenda is sent 10 days before each meeting.
- Written minutes are shared within 5 business days after each meeting.
- A quorum is 8 members, including at least 6 customer members.

## What the council does and does not do

### The council does
- Review roadmap themes.
- Test early designs.
- Rank requests submitted by customers.

### The council does not
- Approve pricing.
- Commit Windrow to a delivery date.
- Replace the normal support channel. Support issues continue to go through support.

## Confidentiality

- All members sign a mutual non-disclosure agreement before the first meeting.
- Roadmap material shown to the council is confidential unless it is marked otherwise.
